The High Road
A busy London high road under a low sky: a newsagent, a tube station sign with
its mouth open, a television studio with a glass front and a smaller sign over
the door, and, to the north, the Dancing Gnu, whose door is shut. The park is
west and the press pen back by the passage southwest.

You can see a kebab wrapper and a snail here.

Ford ambles in after you, towel over one shoulder.

A man in a damp raincoat stands a little way off, looking at you as one looks at
a train one has been waiting for.

>examine kebab wrapper
A crumpled kebab wrapper, dropped in the gutter by someone who did not like it
but ate it anyway. A coin you cannot place is stuck in the grease. The wrapper
has a scrawl on it in biro: a small, angry arrow pointing down the road to the
Tube.

[The score has just gone up by three points.]

