The Tube Station
A tube station entrance, a flight of steps, a ticket hall and a bank of barriers
that have been told not to let anyone through. A map hangs on the wall. The
platforms lead off east (Platform 1) and west (Platform 2). The High Road is
back to the north.

The departure board flickers as you pass under it, and quietly reorders itself.
The cube in your pocket is warm.

You can see a ticket stub here.

Ford ambles in after you, towel over one shoulder.

A man in a damp raincoat stands a little way off, looking at you as one looks at
a train one has been waiting for.

>examine ticket stub
A torn ticket stub caught in the barrier, the sort of thing that is dropped by
someone who jumped it. On the back, in the same angry biro as the wrapper, is a
single word, underlined twice: DOWN. And a number: 2.

[The score has just gone up by four points.]

