>ask tricia about broadcast
"Ninety seconds at ten past," says Tricia, "and the autocue is yours. Say what
you want to say. I'll hold the floor manager. If this turns out to be a mistake,
I'd like it on record that I was very reasonable."

>examine autocue
You step onto the set at the marked moment, and the screen scrolls the words
that Tricia has cleared: DON'T PANIC. IT IS NOT WHAT YOU THINK. THERE IS A PUB
ON THE HIGH ROAD. GO HOME. A cameraman, who has seen a great deal of television,
nods slowly. Across the city, an unusually large number of people put their
coats on.

