Tricia's Flat
A tidy, bookish flat on the first floor above the studio, all shelves and stubby
candles and an enormous plant at the window. A framed photograph stands on the
mantelpiece. A small dish on the bookshelf holds a single earring. The studio
lobby is back to the north.

You can see a framed photograph and a silver earring here.

Ford ambles in after you, towel over one shoulder.

Tricia follows, taking in the place with a journalist's eye.

>examine photo
A faded print of a party in a crowded room in Islington: wine, laughter, an
enormous plant. At the back, slightly out of focus, stands a young man in a
bathrobe with the expression of someone who has just not said the right thing.
You have never seen the picture. You know the room.

[The score has just gone up by four points.]

>examine earring
A small silver earring, delicate and slightly unfashionable, a thing someone
chose with care. You have seen its twin. Trillian wore one exactly like it, on
Lamuella, an hour ago, or a lifetime. This Earth's Tricia has the other half of
the pair.

